docs {
  # Admin List Saved Provider Plans
  
  Returns enabled and disabled SMEAPI, SME Plug, Autopilot, UjayData, Ogdams,
  2Fast, or VTpass plans. Copy a plan's `id` into the `dataPlanId` Bruno
  environment variable before running the update request.

  This endpoint is for admin only. It returns provider names and provider plan
  details so admin can price, enable, disable, filter, and audit plans per
  provider.
  
  Optional query filters:
  
  ```txt
  network=MTN|AIRTEL|GLO|9MOBILE
  type=AWOOF|GIFTING|SME|CORPORATE GIFTING|DATA SHARE|SOCIAL|OTHER
  isEnabled=true|false
  providerAvailable=true|false
  customerVisible=true|false
  provider=smeapi|smeplug|autopilot|ujaydata|ogdams|2fast|vtpass
  sortBy=provider|network|price|name
  sortDirection=asc|desc
  ```

  ## Filter Meaning

  `provider`
  Returns plans from one provider only. Use this when admin wants to manage
  SMEAPI, 2Fast, SME Plug, UjayData, Ogdams, Autopilot, or VTpass separately.

  `network`
  Returns plans for one mobile network only.

  `isEnabled`
  Filters by BillXpress enablement. `isEnabled=true` means admin enabled the
  plan in BillXpress, but it does not always mean the customer can see it. The
  provider also has to be active for that network in data settings.

  `providerAvailable`
  Filters by upstream provider availability from the last sync. A plan must be
  provider-available before customers can see or buy it.

  `customerVisible`
  Returns plans that are visible to customers right now. This combines:

  - `isEnabled=true`;
  - the plan's provider is selected for that plan's network in data settings;
  - if the provider marked the plan unavailable, `available` will be false.

  Use `customerVisible=true` for the admin screen that previews what users can
  currently see in the app. This is different from `isEnabled=true`, because
  `isEnabled=true` can include enabled plans from providers that are saved but
  not currently selected for the network.

  `sortBy`
  Sorts the admin list. Recommended default is `provider`, so all enabled plans
  are grouped by provider when more than one provider is active.
  
  Example:
  
  ```txt
  /api/v1/admin/services/data/plans?provider=smeplug&network=AIRTEL&type=AWOOF
  ```
  
  For SMEAPI MTN plans:
  
  ```txt
  /api/v1/admin/services/data/plans?provider=smeapi&network=MTN
  ```

  For all plans currently visible to customers across the configured providers:

  ```txt
  /api/v1/admin/services/data/plans?customerVisible=true&sortBy=provider
  ```

  For customer-visible plans from one provider:

  ```txt
  /api/v1/admin/services/data/plans?customerVisible=true&provider=2fast
  ```

  For all BillXpress-enabled plans from every provider, whether or not the
  provider is currently selected for that network:

  ```txt
  /api/v1/admin/services/data/plans?isEnabled=true&sortBy=provider
  ```

  For all enabled MTN plans from every provider:

  ```txt
  /api/v1/admin/services/data/plans?network=MTN&isEnabled=true&sortBy=provider
  ```

  For customer-visible MTN plans only:

  ```txt
  /api/v1/admin/services/data/plans?network=MTN&customerVisible=true&sortBy=provider
  ```

  For MTN 2Fast datashare inventory plans:

  ```txt
  /api/v1/admin/services/data/plans?provider=2fast&network=MTN&type=DATA%20SHARE
  ```
  
  For Autopilot MTN plans:
  
  ```txt
  /api/v1/admin/services/data/plans?provider=autopilot&network=MTN
  ```
  
  Admin UI should show:
  
  - provider and network;
  - provider plan name/type/validity;
  - `networkPrice`, `providerPrice`, and `costPrice`;
  - editable `ourPrice` for normal app users;
  - editable `vendorPrice` for API/vendor users;
  - `isEnabled`;
  - `providerAvailable`;
  - `available`, meaning the upstream provider can currently sell the plan;
  - `customerAvailable`, meaning BillXpress enabled the plan and customers can
    currently see/buy it;
  - `lastSyncedAt`.

  The normal customer app must not use this endpoint. It should use:

  ```txt
  GET /api/v1/services/data/plans
  ```

  The customer endpoint hides provider fields. This admin endpoint shows them
  intentionally so admin can understand which provider each saved plan belongs
  to.
  
  `isEnabled` is BillXpress's choice. `providerAvailable` is the upstream
  provider's current status. `available` tracks provider availability.
  `customerAvailable` tracks customer visibility. A plan must satisfy both
  provider availability and BillXpress enablement before customers can see it.
  
  `ourPrice` and `vendorPrice` are optional fixed selling prices. When either is
  set, that exact amount is used for that audience instead of percentage/tier
  markup. Clear a price with `null` to return that audience to fallback markup.
  
  Price fields:
  
  - `networkPrice`: SIM/network hosted cost. Use this when BillXpress is
    vending from its SIM.
  - `providerPrice`: provider wallet/API cost.
  - `costPrice`: effective cost used for fallback markup/profit. When
    `allowHostedSim` is true and `networkPrice` exists, this equals
    `networkPrice`; otherwise it falls back to `providerPrice`.
}
